# Build output
#
# ANCHORED to the repository root, and that matters. An unanchored `build/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, and M6 added `tools/build/` — the derivation graph and build service — which
# git then ignored in its entirety: six thousand lines of source that `git status` did not mention and
# no commit could contain. `/build/` is `build/<profile>/`, which is what CMakePresets.json creates
# and all this line ever meant; a build tree somewhere else is still caught by CMakeCache.txt,
# CMakeFiles/ and _deps/ below.
/build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Swift
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
Package.resolved

# Cooked content and caches
cooked/
.cookcache/
*.cypak

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local overrides
CMakeUserPresets.json
*.local

# --- Build trees and caches -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# `build/<profile>/` is where CMakePresets.json puts every configuration, so `/build/` above covers
# the normal case. What follows covers the tools' own caches and the trees a different entry point
# creates.

# CMake and Ninja
_deps/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
Testing/

# Compiler and build caches
.ccache/
.sccache/
.clangd/
.clang-tidy-cache/

# Cargo, for the editor workspace
target/

# Python, for the tooling that is scripts rather than compiled targets
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Local workflow overrides. `.just.local` and CMakeUserPresets.json are how a contributor configures
# local paths; editing a shared workflow file to do it is a defect against
# `developer-workflow-and-just`.
.just.local
.env.local

# Diagnostic artefacts. Traces and crash reports are written to the user mount, but a run started
# from the repository root will leave them here.
*.cytrace
crash-reports/
perf.data
perf.data.old
.cy-build.lock
